PROBLEM="Structure a 'create order' feature as a self-contained vertical slice (request, handler, result)."
LEARNINGS="VERTICAL SLICE architecture: organize by FEATURE, not by technical layer. Each feature owns its own request (command/query), its handler, and its result type, kept together. The handler is a small focused class with one Handle method that takes the request (+ injected dependencies) and returns the result. Minimal shared abstraction - slices stay independent."
ERRORS="Do NOT spread one feature across global Controllers/Services/Repositories layers (that's layered/n-tier, not vertical slice). Keep the request+handler+result for a feature together; do not force a shared base service."
TAGS="src:context7 lang:csharp area:architecture arch:vertical-slice"
REF_SRC="CreateOrder.cs"
